{
    "background_story": "Solomon was a young Jewish man living in Nazi-occupied France during World War II. As the Gestapo tightened its grip on the city, Solomon's family was forced to go into hiding. With his parents and siblings in danger, Solomon took it upon himself to gather intelligence on the Gestapo's movements and operations. He risked his life daily, sneaking into abandoned buildings and eavesdropping on enemy conversations. The information he gathered was invaluable to the French Resistance, helping them to evade capture and plan daring raids. Solomon's bravery and cunning earned him the codename 'L'Ombre' (The Shadow), and he became a thorn in the side of the Gestapo. Though his actions were shrouded in secrecy, Solomon's contributions to the war effort were instrumental in saving countless lives.",
